<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
  <p><strong>Effective date:</strong> January 1, 2026</p>

  <h2>Informational Use Only</h2>
  <p>All content on nursinghomeneglectcalc.com — including the calculator, guides, methodology, and FAQ — is provided for informational and educational purposes only. Nothing on this site constitutes legal advice or creates a professional relationship. Calculator results are estimates based on documented harm-type baselines and elder abuse statute frameworks; they do not predict outcomes for any specific case.</p>
  <p>Actual nursing home neglect and abuse case outcomes depend on specific facts the calculator cannot know: the specific deficiency citation history of the facility, arbitration clause enforceability, the applicable state elder abuse statute, the quality of medical documentation, Medicaid lien amounts, and case-specific causation evidence. The estimates are educational tools, not legal predictions.</p>

  <h2>No Professional Relationship</h2>
  <p>Use of this site does not create an attorney-client relationship or any other professional relationship.</p>

  <h2>Consult Qualified Professionals</h2>
  <p>For nursing home neglect or abuse situations, consult an elder abuse attorney promptly — evidence is time-sensitive and statute of limitations deadlines are strict. Many elder abuse attorneys work on contingency or under fee-shifting statutes with no upfront cost.</p>

  <h2>Accuracy</h2>
  <p>We strive to keep content current. CMS regulations, elder abuse statutes, and related law change periodically. Verify any information with current primary sources or a qualified attorney.</p>

  <h2>Limitation of Liability</h2>
